# OLIVE BRANCH — local overrides for docker-compose.dev.yml.
#
# Copy this file to .env (untracked — see the repo root .gitignore) and
# fill in real values before running:
#   cd scaffold && docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up -d --build
#
# Never commit the real .env. This file exists because a literal
# SESSION_SECRET and a permanently-on DEV_LOGIN were both committed to
# docker-compose.dev.yml and confirmed as real security findings — anyone
# holding that secret could forge a session for any user or child, with
# escalated:true, entirely offline, and DEV_LOGIN=1 needed no credential at
# all. Docker Compose loads a .env file from this same directory
# automatically for ${VAR} substitution — no extra flag needed.

# Required. Signs every session token this stack issues (HMAC-SHA256).
# Generate a real one, don't reuse this repo's own history, and don't
# reuse it across machines:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
SESSION_SECRET=

# Required. Signs/verifies every GET /media/:key?exp=&sig= signed URL
# (server/routes.mjs's defaultMediaStorage). Without a persisted value here,
# a fresh random secret was minted every process start — every outstanding
# signed URL silently 403'd on the next restart, a real finding this project's
# own post-tier audit caught.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
MEDIA_SIGNING_SECRET=

# Opt-in only, default off. Set to 1 to enable POST /v1/auth/dev-login,
# which mints a real, fully valid session for any {userId} or {childId}
# with NO credential check at all — see server/index.mjs's own header.
# This is what physical-device testing needs; leave it 0 (or unset)
# anywhere this stack might be reachable by anyone but you.
DEV_LOGIN=0

# MASTERFILE §16.2 #6 REVERSED AGAIN — required for any real call. Create a
# free project at https://cloud.livekit.io, then copy its WebSocket URL and
# an API key/secret pair here. Both `server` and `callroom` (docker-compose
# .dev.yml) read these; without all three, a real call attempt fails loudly
# (500 call_backend_unconfigured) rather than degrading onto infrastructure
# nobody chose. No LAN-IP dev default exists here on purpose, unlike the
# old self-hosted-Jitsi-era JITSI_SERVER_URL this replaced — a managed
# cloud service has no meaningful "dev machine's own address" fallback.
LIVEKIT_URL=
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=

# Optional. Overrides the `db` service's Postgres superuser password
# (defaults to the literal "postgres" if left unset, matching this stack's
# behavior before this variable existed). The `db` service's own port is
# loopback-only (see docker-compose.dev.yml), so this password is no
# longer reachable from the LAN/WiFi the way it was when that port was
# published on every host interface — but seed-dev.mjs still fills this
# database with real-shaped family data (a child's name and birth date, a
# guardian identity, an active custody-order pattern, a delivered
# video-message artifact), so set a real one here if you want this
# credential to be more than a formality even against another local
# process on the same host.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
